      "descriptionMarkdown": "**The epic spec claims scrollbar-repeat coverage that does not exist.**\n\n- **Expected:** the recorded task and check descriptions match what the test group asserts.\n- **Observed:** the t02 description lists \"scrollbar repeat cadence\" among the asserted behaviours, and the `check-motion-clock` description says \"scrollbar repeat\" is driven by `advance_clock`. `deterministic_motion_clock.rs` has no scrollbar test, and correctly so: gpui owns no scrollbar timer or repeat state machine.\n  - Scrollbar chrome is consumer-owned.\n  - gpui only publishes `ScrollHandle` thumb offsets in the input turn (`ScrollMutationSource::Scrollbar`, `begin/end_scrollbar_drag`), which reads no time.\n  - No timer or repeat logic exists in `div.rs`, `list.rs` or `uniform_list.rs`.\n  \n  The CLOCK-1 item \"scrollbar timers and repeat\" is therefore legitimately vacuous. The spec still overstates what is covered.\n- **Repair:** spec only. Amend the t02 and `check-motion-clock` descriptions, and the CLOCK-1 bullet, to record that gpui has no scrollbar timer or repeat state machine (consumer-owned chrome, time-free thumb publication). Remove \"scrollbar repeat\" from the claimed coverage. No code change.\n\n**Resolved:** plan revision 4 amends the CLOCK-1 bullet and the t02 and `check-motion-clock` descriptions to state that gpui has no scrollbar timer or repeat of its own. No coverage obligation changed.",
